   </condition>
  </conditions>
  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number physical assets made more resilient to climate variability and change, considering human benefits
1. Value of physical assets made more resilient to climate variability and change, considering human benefits
2. Use by vulnerable households, communities, businesses and public sector services of Fund supported tools, instruments, strategies and activities to respond to climate change and variability.
3. Number of males and females (and percentage of total population) reached by climate related early warning systems established/ strengthened  
4. Number of sectoral plans and studies developed and/or adopted aligned to the IWMP.
5. Number of technical and extension officers trained on flood-related EWS data collection and interpretation
6. Number of people benefit from improved flood management through implementation of hard and soft measures for protection of community assets (set by gender) 
7. Number of people reached by flood -related early warning systems established (separate by gender).
8. Number of households served with flood-proofed drainage in Vaisigano River Catchment</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2017">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number single engineered river works solutions to minimize and to withstand flooding exists in Segments 2, 3 and 4 in the Vaisigano River.
2. Currently, residents and economic assets located in the AUA lack protection from extreme flooding of the Vaisigano River
3. Currently the EWS covers only tsunami and earthquake warnings
4. Limited number of sectoral plans and projects to centrally plan drainage. No feasibility studies prepared for better rain and wastewater storage.
5. Limited capacity exists for technicians to interpret early warning data instruments and utilize for flood related response
6. Number of people benefit from flood management from climate resilient flood protection measures introduced in Vaisigano River catchment for protection of community assets. 
7. The current EWS does not cover floods.
8. Currently, hazard areas exist within the AUA have inadequate drainage systems to withstand high volumes of water</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Drainage master plan completed
2. PES framework in place
3. Mid Term Review completed
4. Channelization of segment 2,3 &amp; 4 completed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Drainage Sites 1-20 Upgrade Designs completed
2. PES Framework Design completed
3. Interim Evaluation completed 
4. Designs of Segments 2, 3, &amp; 4 completed

The only 4 reporting results as planned in 2020 AWP which are related to Indicator 1, 6 and 8.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Close tender for the upgrade of the Lelata Bridge works and conduct evaluation
2. Finalize LARAP and ESMP for the Lelata Bridge works
3. Finalize and endorsed APR 2020
4. Project Implementation Specialist on board
5. Award contract for the Upgrade of the Lelata Bridge works
6. LARAP, LAAP and ESMP approved and operational
7. ISS functional and operational</narrative>
